Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 14:19:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Knowledge: the eighth judgement round's defects

Two rules of the last round had no test: a repository that has commits is not given a new manifest, and doctor lists a link or a file at a fixed scope's name with and without a database. Both are held now. rebuild refuses, forgetting nothing, where the data directory has no knowledge folder at all and the index holds repositories: the rows are another data directory's until the person says otherwise. The root's taxonomy is no longer read through a link at the root's name. The rule on asking the disk is worded for the places that keep it, and the limits it leaves are stated in ADR 0024.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
